{
  "title": "ClassroomIO \u2014 edtech (1,546\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: ClassroomIO\nDomain: edtech | Scale: medium | Stars: 1,546\nProblem: ClassroomIO is an open-source learning management system that provides a simple, beautiful alternative to proprietary platforms like Moodle, EdX, and Teachable. It empowers bootcamps, educators, and businesses to manage training programs and deliver high-quality education at scale without vendor lock-in.\nTarget users: Bootcamp instructors, Corporate trainers, Independent educators, Educational organizations, Companies running internal training programs\nCore features: Advanced Course Management (unlimited courses, lessons, assignments, grading, certificates); Multi-teacher organization management with course assignment; AI-powered course content generation using OpenAI; Community forum for student questions and peer support; Mobile-first student dashboard with course access; Self-hosting capability with full open-source stack\nIntegrations: OpenAI (course and assignment generation), Better Auth (authentication), Hono (HTTP framework)\nTech stack: SvelteKit, Svelte, TailwindCSS + Hono, Node.js + PostgreSQL + Docker, Redis, Turbo monorepo\nKey libraries: Better Auth, TailwindCSS, Prettier, Lefthook, Turbo\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo strategy (Turbo) enables modular separation of concerns: website, dashboard, API, docs, and shared packages (db, utils, ui) for code reuse\n- Full-stack TypeScript adoption across frontend (Svelte/SvelteKit) and backend (Hono) reduces context switching and improves type safety\n- Self-hosting capability is a core differentiator; architecture supports both cloud and on-premise deployments via environment configuration and license keys\n- Multi-tenant design with organization and course-level permissions built in; asynchronous job processing (Redis/jobs-worker) handles resource-intensive tasks like PDF/video processing separately",
